  "security_implications": "The iv_q register stores the Initialization Vector (IV) for AES modes (e.g., CBC, CTR). Corruption of the IV due to incorrect iv_we control or untimely reset can lead to deterministic keystream reuse (if IV repeats) or incorrect decryption, breaking confidentiality or integrity. The chunk uses parameterized slices (NumSlicesCtr) and a condition-based write (iv_we == SP2V_HIGH), so any mismatch in parameter widths or write condition could introduce silent IV corruption.",
